  "id": "tutorial",
  "title": "First weeks at the hub",
  "summary": "Tutorial. The hub island only, 16 days, 300 personnel, already open with the basics running. Three requests arrive on days 1, 4 and 9: bottled water while the water point is down in a heat advisory, a forklift rental after the host nation takes its forklifts back, and a waste contract when the host nation pulls its honey trucks. Each teaches one instrument: a card or cash buy (who takes which, and cash on hand), a BPA call the vendor turns down (a BPA is not a promise), and a written purchase order with a COR (a service needs terms). In the second half the dining contractor slips two days running and the COR reports it, so every play meets the decision on a contractor who slips (D31). The outgoing contracting officer stays three days as the mentor.",
